# IL5 MLOps Feedback Loop: Brief

**Flow:** Source systems → Synapse pipelines → ADLS Gen2 (raw → curated → feature → feedback zones) → Azure ML (Dev/Test-Stage/Prod workspaces) → deployed endpoint → inference + human-reviewed feedback → back into feature zone → scheduled retrain.

## Stage → Azure service

| Stage | Services | Gov note |
|---|---|---|
| Develop | AML compute instances, AML Environments, ACR | CI/CD control plane issue: see risks |
| Train | AML Pipelines, compute clusters, MLflow | GA |
| Validate/Test | Custom eval steps + Fairlearn/InterpretML | Responsible AI dashboard **not available** in Gov |
| Deploy | Model Registry, managed online + batch endpoints | Managed-VNet isolation still preview in Gov |
| Monitor | Azure Monitor, App Insights, Sentinel | GA |
| Feedback/re-loop | ADLS feedback zone, scheduled AML pipeline recurrence | Don't rely on Event Grid trigger: preview-only |

## Core IL5 controls

- **Region:** IL5 = Azure Government only (not Gov Secret/IL6); 5 authorized regions: US Gov AZ/TX/VA (need Dedicated Host or isolated VM SKUs) vs. US DoD Central/East (no extra config, physically separated).
- **Encryption:** CMK/HSM via Key Vault on all storage: must be enabled *before* first write.
- **Network/identity:** Private endpoints, no public egress, Entra ID Gov + RBAC + PIM, role split between data scientists / ML engineers / approvers.
- **Governance gate:** Recorded human approval before Test→Prod promotion, backed by the Fairlearn/InterpretML report.
- **Lineage:** Purview (Gov: US Gov Virginia only): but Synapse pipeline lineage isn't auto-captured in Gov; needs a compensating control.

## Top risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Synapse→Purview lineage not auto-captured in Gov | Push lineage via Atlas API, or maintain a manual per-dataset manifest |
| Responsible AI dashboard unavailable in Gov | Fairlearn/InterpretML as pipeline step, reviewed at approval gate |
| Azure DevOps Services/GitHub Enterprise Cloud sit outside the IL5 boundary (GH Gov is only FedRAMP Moderate) | Self-hosted agents/server inside the Gov VNet; ISSO sign-off on the pattern |
| Managed-VNet isolation for online endpoints is preview in Gov | Use customer-VNet injection + private endpoints instead |
| CMK can't be applied retroactively | Gate go-live on a "CMK verified" IaC check |

## Open questions to confirm before build

Batch vs. real-time inference; model type (classical ML vs. generative); target region (IL5 vs IL6); existing Purview/Sentinel/CI-CD already under this ATO; Feature Store's actual Gov availability (unconfirmed: fallback is versioned tables in the feature zone).

